      "Transcription:\n",
      "--------------------------------------------------\n",
      "So RAG, it stands for Retrieval Augmented Generation. And essentially, it is a framework. And what it does, it enhances the capabilities of your large language model of your LLMs. And it actually does that by integrating your private knowledge bases. And this way, it improves your factual accuracy and also your contextual relevance. Now, in RAG, there are three main phases, ingestion, retrieval, and also generation. So in ingestion, basically what you're doing, you're populating your vector database. That's what your ingestion consists of. In retrieval, you retrieve the chunks from the vector DB, and you retrieve only those chunks that's relevant to answering the question. On the other hand, in generation, you are generating the answer from the chunks you received from the previous step. So that's the idea of your rag.\n"
     ]
